1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,506
You've tuned the viewer.

2
00:00:01,566 --> 00:00:06,058
Now, how do you know it looks right where
it actually matters — on your storefront?

3
00:00:06,118 --> 00:00:09,459
There are three tools, and they do
genuinely different things.

4
00:00:10,669 --> 00:00:15,100
Three buttons in the header. Preview, Save
settings, and Save And View.

5
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:18,389
People mix these up constantly, so let's
be precise.

6
00:00:19,249 --> 00:00:21,309
First, the live preview on the right.

7
00:00:21,369 --> 00:00:24,404
It updates as you drag, and it needs no
button at all.

8
00:00:24,464 --> 00:00:27,211
This is where you do ninety percent of
your work.

9
00:00:27,271 --> 00:00:31,738
It's the same viewer code the storefront
runs, loading the same file — so if it

10
00:00:31,798 --> 00:00:34,202
looks right here, it will look right
there.

11
00:00:35,062 --> 00:00:36,524
Second, the Preview button.

12
00:00:36,584 --> 00:00:40,976
This opens your actual storefront product
page and applies your unsaved changes

13
00:00:41,036 --> 00:00:41,878
through the URL.

14
00:00:41,938 --> 00:00:46,499
Nothing is written to your store — close
the tab and it's as if it never happened.

15
00:00:47,359 --> 00:00:51,822
So you see your dark background, your
camera angle, your control bar — inside

16
00:00:51,882 --> 00:00:55,757
your real theme, with your real header,
fonts and layout around it.

17
00:00:55,817 --> 00:01:00,398
That context is the whole point. Nothing
about your saved settings has changed.

18
00:01:01,258 --> 00:01:05,870
Use Preview while you're still deciding —
try five backgrounds against your real

19
00:01:05,930 --> 00:01:07,739
page without writing five times.

20
00:01:07,799 --> 00:01:09,549
When you've decided, then save.

21
00:01:10,409 --> 00:01:13,539
Save settings writes the config to the
product's metafield.

22
00:01:13,599 --> 00:01:16,134
That's the moment it becomes real for
customers.

23
00:01:16,994 --> 00:01:20,549
You get a confirmation, and the button
goes back to reading Saved.

24
00:01:21,259 --> 00:01:25,273
Save And View is the convenience button,
and it does something subtle.

25
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:28,766
It saves, then it waits, and only then
opens the storefront.

26
00:01:28,826 --> 00:01:30,745
The waiting is the important part.

27
00:01:31,605 --> 00:01:35,864
Shopify takes a few seconds to propagate a
metafield write to the storefront.

28
00:01:35,924 --> 00:01:40,294
If you opened the page immediately you'd
see your old settings and conclude the

29
00:01:40,354 --> 00:01:41,192
save had failed.

30
00:01:41,252 --> 00:01:45,679
So the app opens a placeholder tab with
this spinner, holds it for a moment, and

31
00:01:45,739 --> 00:01:46,520
then navigates.

32
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:49,283
And there's the published result.

33
00:01:49,343 --> 00:01:53,209
This is what a customer will load — saved
settings, no URL tricks.

34
00:01:53,269 --> 00:01:55,351
If it looks right here, you're done.

35
00:01:56,211 --> 00:02:00,688
Occasionally a hard reload is still needed
— caching happens at several layers.

36
00:02:00,748 --> 00:02:05,226
If the storefront keeps ignoring your
changes, check the Setup page: storefront

37
00:02:05,286 --> 00:02:09,362
read access has to be on, or your theme
literally can't read the config.

38
00:02:09,422 --> 00:02:14,072
And if no tab opens at all, your browser
blocked the pop-up — both buttons need to

39
00:02:14,132 --> 00:02:15,106
be a direct click.

40
00:02:15,966 --> 00:02:20,998
Next up, the 3D Model Library — for models
that don't belong to a single product.
